			"notes": "## Lightsabers 0.4.0\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Updated to Minecraft Java 26.3, Fabric Loader 0.19.5, and Fabric API 0.162.0+26.3.\n- Real independent dual-wield attacks: with two lightsabers equipped, right mouse controls the physical right hand and left mouse controls the physical left hand, including left-handed settings.\n- Each saber has its own swing animation, sound, damage, durability, and cooldown. Targets and reach are validated on the server.\n- Added a soft, color-matched aura to all six blade colors, with a gentle two-second pulse and full-bright blades. Works without shaders and alongside Iris; normal sabers no longer force an enchantment glint.\n- Fixed independent cooldowns and durability for dual-wielded blasters, and corrected Jedi tunic fall protection.\n- Added the pinned Gradle wrapper, regression tests, refreshed development setup, and a release workflow that publishes the verified build artifacts.\n\n### Installation\n\n- Use `lightsabers-0.4.0.jar`; the sources jar is for development, not installation.\n- Requires Minecraft Java **26.3**, Java **25**, Fabric Loader **0.19.5 or newer**, and compatible Fabric API **0.162.0+26.3 or newer**.\n- Install the same mod version on the Fabric server and all joining clients.\n- Sodium, Iris, LambDynamicLights, Mod Menu, and shader packs are optional client-side visual enhancements. The blade aura itself does not require them.\n\nThis release is not compatible with Minecraft 26.1.2. Back up worlds before upgrading.\n\n### Verification\n\n- Clean build, 12 unit tests, and 5 required server GameTests passed.\n- Client rendering and input tests passed both without shaders and with the installed Iris/Sodium visual stack."
		},
